{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457418-question-on-goblin-fruit","id":1457418,"title":"question on goblin fruit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-22T13:06:47-07:00","id":1457418,"title":"question on goblin fruit","content":"quick question, can the true fae use goblin fruits. i kinda picture the gentry relaxing in there mad palaces eating goblin fruits or being fed them ala roman emperors. am i right, or is there the bane and boon of the hedge's produce to arcadia's rulers just as it does to those warped by the durance?<br /> <br /> also, following that train of thought, are any of the splats besides changelings affected by goblin fruits and oddments? can a werewolf or a beast eat a goblin fruit and gain powers or does it just not work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T15:00:35-07:00","id":1457428,"title":"","content":"From my understanding anyone who eats a goblin fruits receives the effects and anyone can use oddments.<br /> I have yet to read second edition, but I really can't imagine this changing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T15:31:26-07:00","id":1457429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457418-question-on-goblin-fruit?p=1457428#post1457428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my understanding anyone who eats a goblin fruits receives the effects and anyone can use oddments.<br /> I have yet to read second edition, but I really can't imagine this changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, ok. <br /> <br /> i still see the whole &quot;Gentry eating goblin fruit like grapes&quot; thing. you know, reclining in decedance and not really being affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:23:22-07:00","id":1457439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457418-question-on-goblin-fruit?p=1457429#post1457429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm, ok.<br /> <br /> i still see the whole &quot;Gentry eating goblin fruit like grapes&quot; thing. you know, reclining in decedance and not really being affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's a cool image.<br /> <br /> just a little positive affirmation for you;<br /> If you like something, rules be damned don't let anyone tell you how to play, it's your game play it your way. (Assuming your the ST)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:38:04-07:00","id":1457442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457418-question-on-goblin-fruit?p=1457439#post1457439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it's a cool image.<br /> <br /> just a little positive affirmation for you;<br /> If you like something, rules be damned don't let anyone tell you how to play, it's your game play it your way. (Assuming your the ST)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>thanks. i am not playing the game, but just seems like something a gentry would do, ya know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T05:59:20-07:00","id":1457703,"title":"","content":"That's the thing.<br /> <br /> In their own world, where their stats barely matter, of COURSE they indulge themselves. The petty changeling watches and thinks &quot;god, if only I had a +2 stength, or a fruit that can heal aggravated damage&quot; (abstractly, of course). The true Fae don't need it in Arcadia. Their stats are already so high its almost silly for them to eat Goblin Fruit for any other reason than to say &quot;if I can't have it,no one will&quot; and &quot;neener neener, I have it and you don't&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's Arcadia. In the Hedge, I imagine the fae take their indulgences with them. They're on the Border, and some mortal things trouble them. They'll likely try to bring a veritable feast, and leave their Changelings and Hobgoblins to figure out how to preserve and transfer it. Here, they might need it, thus they're likely to horde whatever goblin fruit helps with their current side quest.<br /> <br /> Those trapped in the mortal plane are a bit more pressed. While they don't NEED goblin fruit or flesh in the mortal realm, many of them didn't realize how difficult the human world is. Many might be willing to make a deal for a goblin fruit they forgot to being with them. In a desert, a drop of water isnworth more than a diamond to the right person","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 08-26-2021, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T07:45:17-07:00","id":1457709,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar935_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"935\" data-vbnamecard=\"935\">Cleverest of Things</a>, that is a great idea! I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T22:49:48-07:00","id":1458021,"title":"","content":"A True Fae somewhere does exactly that. But nothing is true to all of them, or even to most of them. They are living stories, and in their own realms in Arcadia they're the literal law of the land. Their only weakness there is that there is no story without conflict, and it isn't a true conflict if the result is predictable, both sides always have a chance. That's how Changelings escape in the first place.<br /> <br /> On the Hedge things start to change drastically, but they are still too at home for many changelings to notice. Indeed, they're too at home to notice it themselves, which is actually a big boon against them if you have the means to explore it. Their particular stance on Goblin Fruits may change, but it will still be more based on their identities than on any sense of need. A Hunter may hoard and sparingly consume GFs in the Hedge because it is what a Hunter does in the wild. A King may have an entourage carrying and picking savory fruits because that's what a King does. A Scientist will get samples and experiment on them, even feeding them to subjects instead of ever consuming them, because that's what a Scientist does.<br /> <br /> But once they're on Earth, everything depends on how much time they stay. Earth is as changing to the True Fae as Arcadia to humans and mundane objects. So with time they can start to really think in practical terms instead of in their Story terms and consider GFs carefully. This is particularly true for exiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T04:05:19-07:00","id":1458047,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> that is so good! i love that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}